Single-database configuration for Flask.

Run these from the `backend/` directory with `FLASK_APP=main.py`:

    flask db upgrade                       # apply migrations (also run by deploy.sh)
    flask db migrate -m "describe change"  # create a new migration after editing models

Do not run `flask db init`; this directory already exists.

A development database that `create_all` built has no Alembic revision, and neither command works
on it as it is: delete it, or stamp it first. See "Development databases" in
docs/infrastructure_and_devops.md.

This is the only supported way to change the schema. Production is upgraded by deploy.sh in this
order: backup, bootstrap/stamp check, `flask db upgrade`, `flask seed`. The root revision is an
empty placeholder, so the history cannot build a database from scratch; a brand-new database is
created from the models and stamped to head by deploy.sh.

Rules:
- Schema changes only via `flask db migrate`; there must be a single head (`flask db heads`).
- No raw-SQL or one-off database scripts.
- Data fixes go in an Alembic data migration; data every install needs is an idempotent upsert in
  `flask seed`. tools/migrate_classroom.py is retired and must not gain new steps.

See the "Database upgrade path" in docs/infrastructure_and_devops.md.
